    ‖trigPoly c t‖ = ‖∑ k ∈ c.support, c k • mFourier k t‖ := rfl
    _ ≤ ∑ k ∈ c.support, ‖c k • mFourier k t‖ := norm_sum_le _ _  -- norm_finset_sum? norm_sum_le
    _ = ∑ k ∈ c.support, ‖c k‖ := by
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun k hk => ?_)
        rw [norm_smul, UnitAddTorus.mFourier_norm?, mul_one] -- ‖c k • mFourier k t‖ = ‖c k‖ * ‖mFourier k t‖ = ‖c k‖ * 1 — hmm ‖mFourier k t‖ = 1: pointwise — from fourierMode_abs_eq_one via compat — or mFourier_norm gives the C-norm 1 → pointwise ≤ 1 — I need = 1: ‖mFourier k t‖ = 1: mFourier is a product of fourier: ‖∏ fourier‖ = ∏ ‖fourier‖ = 1 [norm_prod ✓ + ‖fourier n t‖ = 1 — `fourier_norm`? there's `AddCircle.fourier_norm`? hmm — probe `#check fourier_norm`. OR use my own: mFourier k t = fourierMode k rep... Basic has torusFourier_abs_eq_one/fourierMode_abs_eq_one — UT-side: ‖mFourier k t‖ — via fourierMode_abs_eq_one + compat: fourierMode k rep = mFourier k (torusQuot rep) = mFourier k t ✓. So ‖mFourier k t‖ = 1 via fourierMode_abs_eq_one ✓.
  -- then Cauchy–Schwarz:
  _ = ∑ k ∈ c.support, (sobolevWeightHalf s k * ‖c k‖) * (1 + normSq k) ^ (-(s/2)) := by
      -- ‖c k‖ = (1+|k|²)^{s/2}·‖c k‖ · (1+|k|²)^{-s/2}
